BUG-48: a Writer document with a comment trapped the headless engine ("memory access out of bounds").

Since Writer got a real SwView (FG-096, #419, 2026-10-04) every view makes a SwPostItMgr. It collects the
document's comments (SwPostItMgr::InsertItem) and, once the event loop turns, lays them out from a posted user
event, which creates one SwAnnotationWin per comment: a widget built from annotation.ui, a UI file the slimmed
VFS does not contain. The headless engine has no sidebar to show them in. Every DOCX, ODT, DOC or RTF that carried
a comment failed to convert while the same text without a comment converted.

InsertItem now declines to register the comment in the sidebar list, so nothing is laid out. The comment itself
stays in the document model, which is what the exports read, so editable outputs keep their comments.
CONSEQUENCE, repeated in the code: everything that reads the sidebar list is empty too, in particular PDF export of
comments in the margin (ExportNotesInMargin prints through this manager). The build offers no such option.

Module-scoped (-documents): pdf-docx also links Writer and gives it a view, but PDF import creates no comment, so
its manager has none to lay out.

